 - **The asker hears the answer.** When a task with a `from` completes, `hooks.answered` sends the asker the outcome in one line.
 - **Which adds count as requests:** an add counts when the caller is not the log's own agent (the task's `agent`). Tasks an agent adds to its own log are not requests. Adds by the owner (from the browser) and by a parent adding steps to its child's task count too, so each one sends the receiver a notice.
 - **Where it is built:** `notify_requests` in `Servex/agents/page_tools.js`; the two hooks are wired in `Servex.js`. Test: `node Servex/agents/requests.test.mjs`.
+- **`from` is overloaded (ask1-origin, 2026-11-03):** a voice-filed task can carry `from: {prompt, sentence}` (the sentence that asked for it; `task_origin()`, readme.md) instead of an asker's agent id. `notify_requests` only ever treats a STRING `from` as an asker — an object `from` is never stamped by the asker-skip check (`a.from === undefined`, page_tools.js), and never reaches `hooks.answered` as a `to`. The tradeoff: a voice-filed task handed off this way gets no automatic "it's done" notice back to the voice session; the mastermind that completes it must tell the owner some other way (a chat line, a card) if that matters. Test: `node Servex/agents/task-origin.test.mjs`.
